raph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Takes the canonical minimum spanning tree (weight, then position, as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"minimumSpanningTree(weight:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), a minimum-weight perfect matching on its odd-degree","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices (","type":"text"},{"code":"minimumWeightMatching","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), and an Eulerian circuit of their union by Hierholzer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from the first vertex, shortcut to the first visit of each vertex. The matching is on the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"complete graph of the odd vertices in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order (pairs i < j lexicographic), and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"circuit’s multigraph lists the tree edges by position, then the matched pairs in that order,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so the tour is determined. At most 3\/2 × the shortest tour when the weights satisfy the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"triangle inequality (not checked).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tours read the simple graph, as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nearestNeighborTour(weight:)"},{"type":"text","text":" documents; nil below three"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices."}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Precondition","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The graph is complete; the sum along a tour fits in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"W"},{"type":"text","text":". When "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"W"},{"type":"text","text":" is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FixedWidthInteger"},{"type":"text","text":", every non-loop edge’s weight satisfies n · (2 · |weight| + 1) ≤"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"W.max \/ 8"},{"type":"text","text":" (the matching’s bound), checked as each weight is read, so a weight beyond it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"traps even on an edge the matching never sees; so n ≤ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"W.max \/ 8"},{"type":"text","text":" (15 vertices for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int8"},{"type":"text","text":"), whatever the weights. An arbitrary-precision integer has no bound."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Complexity","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"O(n³): the matching on up to n vertices; the tree O(n²).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"christofidesTour"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Cycle","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks5CycleV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":">?"}],"role":"symb